## Problem 2 – BankAccount (Constructor Chaining using `this()`)

```java
class BankAccount {

    int accountNumber;
    String accountHolder;
    int balance;

    BankAccount() {
        this(1, "Unknown", 0);
    }

    BankAccount(String accountHolder) {
        this(2, accountHolder, 0);
    }

    BankAccount(String accountHolder, int balance) {
        this(3, accountHolder, balance);
    }

    BankAccount(int accountNumber, String accountHolder, int balance) {
        this.accountNumber = accountNumber;
        this.accountHolder = accountHolder;
        this.balance = balance;
    }

    void display() {
        System.out.println("Account Number : " + accountNumber);
        System.out.println("Account Holder : " + accountHolder);
        System.out.println("Balance        : " + balance);
        System.out.println();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        BankAccount b1 = new BankAccount();
        BankAccount b2 = new BankAccount("Stark");
        BankAccount b3 = new BankAccount("Tony", 35000);

        b1.display();
        b2.display();
        b3.display();
    }
}
```

